#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:18
msgid ""
"The subscript of :math:`l, v` in the governing equations denote **pure "
"liquid** phase and **pure vapour** phase, or **liquid-like superfluid** "
"and **vapour-like superfluid**, respectively. And all symbols are defined"
" in :numref:`tab:symbols:multiphase`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:22
msgid "Darcy's Law"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:24
msgid ""
"\\vec{U_i} = - k \\frac{k_{ri}}{\\mu_i} (\\nabla p -\\rho_i \\vec{g}), i "
"= \\{v, l}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:29
msgid "Conservation of fluid mass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:31
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\partial ( \\varepsilon ( S_l\\rho_l + S_v \\rho_v) )}{\\partial "
"t} = - \\nabla \\cdot (\\vec{U_l} \\rho_l) - \\nabla \\cdot (\\vec{U_v} "
"\\rho_v) - \\nabla \\cdot (\\vec{U_s} \\rho_s) + Q_{H_2O}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:36
msgid "The relation of saturation of each phase is :math:`S_l + S_v =1`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:38
msgid "Conservation of energy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:40
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\partial E}{\\partial t}  = & \\frac{\\partial [\\varepsilon ( "
"S_l \\rho_l h_l + S_v \\rho_v h_v + S_s \\rho_s h_s) + "
"(1-\\varepsilon)\\rho_r C_{pr} T]}{\\partial t} \\\\ = & \\nabla \\cdot "
"(\\lambda_r \\nabla T) - \\nabla \\cdot (\\rho_l \\vec{U_l} h_l) - "
"\\nabla \\cdot (\\rho_v \\vec{U_v} h_v) - \\nabla \\cdot (\\rho_s "
"\\vec{U_s} h_s) + \\\\ & \\frac{\\mu_f}{k} \\parallel \\vec{U} \\parallel"
" ^2 - \\left( \\frac{\\partial ln \\rho_f}{\\partial ln T} \\right)_p "
"\\frac{Dp}{Dt}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:48
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:51
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pressure equation"
msgstr "控制方程组"

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:53
msgid ""
"Subtituting equation :eq:`eq:darcy:multiphase` into equation "
":eq:`eq:conti:multiphase`, we can get the pressure equation,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:55
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\partial ( \\varepsilon \\rho_f )}{\\partial t} = \\nabla \\cdot "
"\\left[( {\\color{red}{\\rho_l k \\frac{k_{rl}}{\\mu_l}}} +  "
"{\\color{red}{ \\rho_v k \\frac{k_{rv}}{\\mu_v}}}) \\nabla p \\right] - "
"\\nabla \\cdot \\left[({\\color{blue}{\\rho_l^2 k "
"\\frac{k_{rl}}{\\mu_l}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\rho_v^2 k "
"\\frac{k_{rv}}{\\mu_v}}}) \\vec{g} \\right]+ Q_{H_2O}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:60
msgid ""
"To simplify the formulation, we define phase mobility :math:`M_i` and "
"gravitational contribution :math:`L_i` as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:62
msgid ""
"M_i &= {\\color{red}{\\rho_i k \\frac{k_{ri}}{\\mu_i}}} \\\\ L_i &= "
"{\\color{blue}{\\rho_i^2 k \\frac{k_{ri}}{\\mu_i}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:68
msgid "we can define two kinds of flux on each face of the compputational grid:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:70
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}   \\phi_p &= ( M_l + M_v) \\nabla p \\cdot \\vec{n} \\\\"
"   \\phi_g &= ( L_l + L_v) \\vec{g} \\cdot \\vec{n} \\\\   \\phi &= "
"\\phi_p + \\phi_g \\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:79
msgid ""
"and the flux of liquid phase can be expressed as :eq:`eq:flux_l:flux_v` "
"(see eq. 20 in :cite:`horgue2015open` )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:81
msgid ""
"\\phi_l = \\frac{M_l}{M_l + M_v} \\phi_p + \\frac{L_l}{L_l + L_v}\\phi_g "
"\\\\ \\phi_v = \\frac{M_v}{M_l + M_v} \\phi_p + \\frac{L_v}{L_l + "
"L_v}\\phi_g"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:87
msgid ""
"In OpenFOAM, solving pressure equation of multiphase problem is similar "
"to the single phase problem. :math:`\\phi_p` can be reconstructed from "
"pressure equation after solving it. And velocity of liquid and vapour "
"phase can be reconstructed from :math:`\\phi_l` and :math:`\\phi_v`, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Models_Equations/HydrothermalMultiPhaseDarcyFoam.rst:93
msgid ""
"How to set value for :math:`\\mu_l` in vapour region and :math:`\\mu_v` "
"in liquid region ? They are set to :code:`inf` at the moment, and "
"variable, e.g. :code:`rAU_l` (:math:`k\\frac{k_{rl}}{\\mu_l}`) will be "
"zero in vapour region. Therefore a tiney value should be add in the "
"denominator in line 53-54 of :numref:`lst:pEqn:multiphase`. **Is there "
"any better solution?**"
msgstr ""

